Title: THE RENEWAL
Credit: A short film from the world of the Bureau of Infernal Affairs
Draft date: 2026-11-16

FADE IN:

INT. BUREAU OF INFERNAL AFFAIRS, ANNEX C - MORNING

A municipal annex in Port Meridian. Grey carpet, humming fluorescent light, a queue number display that has been stuck on 7 for years. Rain taps the high windows.

VENOMSPUR, a very tall and very thin bureaucrat, bald, with pointed ears, round black glasses and red eyes, sits behind a steel desk. He wears a black tailcoat, a red bow tie and a red pocket square. He keeps his hands clasped on the desk, as always.

He stamps a form with a brass stamp. The stamp is chipped on one corner.

VENOMSPUR
(to himself)
Form nine, correctly filed. A rare pleasure.

A thin green folder lands on his desk. It is stamped RENEWAL DUE.

VENOMSPUR (CONT'D)
Aurum. Seventh year. Of course it is.

INT. HOLLOWAY STUDIOS, BOOTH A - NIGHT

A sound-proofed recording booth in Port Meridian. Neon red light on the walls.

KID LANTERN, nineteen, thin and watchful, wears a black bomber jacket with red trim and a gold chain with a round medallion. He holds a microphone in his right hand and keeps the other hand in his pocket. White sneakers.

He raps into the dark, then stops, annoyed with himself.

KID LANTERN
Again. That line sits wrong.

KID LANTERN (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Nobody gets in on talent anymore. Somebody signs for it.

A shadow passes the glass of the booth door. A card slides under it. It reads: NOTICE OF OFFER. BUREAU OF INFERNAL AFFAIRS.

EXT. PORT MERIDIAN WATERFRONT - DAWN

Rain over the harbour. VENOMSPUR walks the pier in a rain-soaked black coat over his tailcoat, an umbrella in one hand. Hardly anyone looks twice at him.

AURUM waits at the end of the pier. He is a hip hop megastar in a red puffer jacket, heavy gold chains and red LED glasses. His sneakers glow orange at the soles. He holds a microphone out of habit, though no one is recording.

AURUM
You people never call before you come.

VENOMSPUR
The Bureau does not call. The Bureau files.

AURUM
(laughing)
Seven years. Feels like last week.

VENOMSPUR
It was precisely seven years. I checked.

INT. AURUM'S PENTHOUSE, LIVING ROOM - DAY

A glass room above the city, gold records on every wall. AURUM sits on a white sofa. VENOMSPUR stands, hands clasped. On the table lies the INSTRUMENT OF FORTUNE, a leather folio with a cracked spine.

AURUM
Same terms. Same everything. Sign me up.

VENOMSPUR
Clause nine. Sunset.

AURUM
What about it?

VENOMSPUR
At each renewal, the signatory may decline. The Bureau must offer. I am offering.

AURUM
(not laughing now)
Nobody declines.

VENOMSPUR
Nobody has asked what happens after. I have a form for that.

He sets down a single page: NOTICE OF SATISFACTION.

INT. HOLLOWAY STUDIOS, BOOTH A - LATER

KID LANTERN holds the NOTICE OF OFFER in his left hand, and his microphone in his right.

VENOMSPUR stands in the doorway, a very tall shadow.

KID LANTERN
You are the guy from the card.

VENOMSPUR
I am the clerk. I process requests. Yours is in the pile.

KID LANTERN
What do I get?

VENOMSPUR
Seven years of the finest sound in the city. Then a renewal.

KID LANTERN
And after that?

VENOMSPUR
That is the question every client forgets to ask.

INT. AURUM'S PENTHOUSE, LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

AURUM, alone now, takes off his red LED glasses and puts them on the table. His eyes are tired. He picks up the pen.

AURUM
(to the empty room)
I made the first record in my mother's kitchen.

He signs the NOTICE OF SATISFACTION. The gold records lose their shine, one by one, in the dark.

INT. BUREAU OF INFERNAL AFFAIRS, ANNEX C - MORNING

The queue display changes from 7 to 8. VENOMSPUR stamps the form. The brass stamp cracks in two.

VENOMSPUR
(softly)
Form closed. Correctly filed.

KID LANTERN stands in front of the desk, holding the NOTICE OF OFFER. He tears it in half and drops it on the desk.

KID LANTERN
I will write my own.

VENOMSPUR
(a rare smile)
That is not covered by any form I know.

EXT. PORT MERIDIAN WATERFRONT - DAWN

The rain has stopped. KID LANTERN walks along the pier, microphone in hand. AURUM, in plain clothes, no chains, sits at the end of the pier and listens.

KID LANTERN
(rapping, low)
No contract in my pocket, no stamp on my name.
Same rain on the harbour, but it sounds different now.

AURUM claps once, slowly.

FADE OUT.

THE END
